    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/05/new-balance-fuelcell-rebel-v5-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The new PEBA/EVA FuelCell and higher 35/29 mm stack deliver a softer, more protective heel-to-forefoot ride, with smooth heel transition and moderate forefoot flexibility.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole has strong bounce/energy return with a good softness-to-responsiveness balance, creating a lively non-plated ride rather than a very snappy plated feel.",
        "Stability: Compared with v4, stability is reduced in lateral movement; the wider/looser midfoot upper can allow foot translation on sharp turns, though the platform is wider and rearfoot structure still provides baseline support.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability is reported as slightly improved over the previous version, but overall longevity is still characterized as average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/05/new-balance-fuelcell-rebel-v5-multi.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The PEBA-blend FuelCell midsole (about 35 mm heel / 29 mm forefoot) is soft underfoot without feeling squishy, gives solid impact protection, and improves heel-to-forefoot flow with less lumpy heel landings.",
        "Responsiveness: Testers report strong foam reactivity and a lively, fast ride for an unplated shoe (tempo to racing capable), though the v5 feels slightly less raw/minimal than older Rebels.",
        "Stability: A major strength for such a light shoe, with improved stability from a stiffer midfoot build, semi-rigid/higher heel counter, better lockdown, and geometry updates that support smoother, more controlled transitions.",
        "Durability: The review does not provide long-term wear results, but added forefoot rubber coverage plus a more reinforced upper and heel construction point to improved material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/new-balance-rebel-v5-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The PEBA-blended FuelCell midsole with +5 mm foam (35 mm heel / 29 mm forefoot) is described as soft, forgiving, and comfortable, with a plush heel feel and a forefoot that feels less flat than v4.",
        "Responsiveness: The PEBA blend plus midsole cavity gives noticeable bounce/energy return, smoother transitions, and a lively toe-off; one note says it can feel slightly too soft for hard speed work.",
        "Stability: It is a neutral shoe but reported to balance bounce with stability; improved heel counter/lockdown and a slightly stiffer platform from added outsole rubber improve control and lateral confidence without becoming a true stability trainer.",
        "Durability: Outsole rubber coverage was increased for better wear life and grip, and reviewers call the outsole more durable; prior Rebel versions had upper fragility, which v5 addresses with upper/heel construction updates."
      ]
    }
  ],
